 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "An equation says that two expressions are equal, for example 2x + 3 = 11. The solution is the value of x that makes it true.\nTo solve, do the same thing to both sides, to get x on its own:\n• x + 5 = 12: subtract 5 from both sides, x = 7.\n• x − 4 = 9: add 4 to both sides, x = 13.\n• 3x = 18: divide both sides by 3, x = 6.\n• x ÷ 4 = 3: multiply both sides by 4, x = 12.\nTwo steps: 2x + 3 = 11. Subtract 3: 2x = 8. Divide by 2: x = 4.\nAlways check: put your answer back in. 2 × 4 + 3 = 11 ✓.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "a": 3,
   "b": 7,
   "c": 22
  },
  "problem": "Solve {poly([a, 'x'], [b, ''])} = {c}, and check the answer.",
  "steps": [
   "Subtract {b} from both sides: {mono(a, 'x')} = {c} − {b} = {c - b}.",
   "Divide both sides by {a}: x = {c - b} ÷ {a} = {(c - b) / a}.",
   "Check: {a} × {(c - b) / a} + {b} = {a * (c - b) / a} + {b} = {c} ✓"
  ],
  "answer": "x = {(c - b) / a}",
  "checks": [
   "(c - b) / a == 5"
  ]
 },
